{title: Swing Low, Sweet Chariot}
{artist: Wallace Willis, before 1862}
{key: G}
{tempo: 70}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: spiritual}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Swing low, sweet [C]chari[G]ot
Coming for to carry me [D]home
[G]Swing low, sweet [C]chari[G]ot
Coming for to [D]carry me [G]home

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]looked over Jordan, and [C]what did I [G]see
Coming for to carry me [D]home
A [G]band of angels [C]coming after [G]me
Coming for to [D]carry me [G]home

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If [G]you get there be[C]fore I [G]do
Coming for to carry me [D]home
Tell [G]all my friends I'm [C]coming [G]too
Coming for to [D]carry me [G]home

{chorus}
